OL,3,T///,/,-.,./,,-,-,-.-.,-.,/-.-.,.,.,,///
OL,4,CUS Army says controlled blast of       
OL,5,Cexplosives in Iowa was 'huge success'  
OL,6,GThe US Army says a controlled blast of 
OL,7,Gdegraded explosives in Middletown,     
OL,8,GIowa was a "huge success".             
OL,10,FSmoke could be seen rising into the    
OL,11,Fsky shortly after 09:00 local time -   
OL,12,Fin a news conference afterwards, Maj   
OL,13,FGen Eric Shirley says the army reduced 
OL,14,Fthe risk "as close to zero as is       
OL,15,Fabsolute humanly possible".            
OL,17,FThe controlled detonation of lead      
OL,18,Fazide - a highly volatile compound -   
OL,19,Fwas necessary to prevent an unplanned  
OL,20,Fexplosion, the army says.              
OL,22,                                   G1/2 
